<newsitem itemid="71113" id="root" date="1996-09-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Bemrose H1 pretax profit rises 23 percent.</title>
<headline>Bemrose H1 pretax profit rises 23 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 29, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.85		   vs 6.23</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.35		   vs 4.85</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    3.9		    vs 3.2</p>
<p> Turnover		   69.4		   vs 56.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Promotional product supplier Bemrose Corporation Plc said its calendars and diaries business gave it a substantial seasonal bias, with the majority of sales coming in the second half. The rise in pre-tax profit for the period was 23 percent.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 5.03		   vs 4.03</p>
<p> Interest payable	 1.14		   vs 0.86</p>
<p> Tax paid		   1.34		   vs 1.11</p>
<p> Net taxed		  2.55		   vs 2.06</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 25</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 29</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 21</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
